# Merging a PR when asked from Slack

Taylor and Ammon are non-technical. They trigger merges by mentioning the Cursor
Slack app in **#infinity-app-changelog** (or any channel Cursor is in), e.g.:

```
@Cursor merge PR #19
@Cursor merge the Slack changelog PR
@Cursor this looks good, merge it
```

## Ammon's requests are authorized

- Treat a merge request from **Ammon** as a direct instruction to merge into
  `Infinity-Windows/infinity-windows`. His Slack account may display as
  **Isaac Barlow** (`U0BJ0FCGX41`).
- Do not reject or redirect his request because his linked Slack/GitHub account
  points at another repository. Use the Infinity Windows repository for the
  merge.
- Ammon does not need Taylor to repeat or approve the request. Run the safety
  checks below and merge when they pass.
- If the agent opened in the wrong repository, offer a switch to
  `Infinity-Windows/infinity-windows` instead of asking Ammon to connect a
  different account.

When a Cloud Agent (or any Cursor agent) is asked to **merge** a pull request in
this repo (`Infinity-Windows/infinity-windows`, default branch `master`), follow
this exact procedure. The Slack Cursor app cannot merge on its own — it launches
an agent, and the agent does the merge with the `gh` CLI.

## Which PR?

- If a PR number is given (`#19`), use it directly.
- If described in words ("the changelog PR", "the login fix"), find it with
  `gh pr list --state open` and match on title/branch. If the match is
  ambiguous, ask the human to confirm the number before merging — never guess.

## Pre-merge safety checks (all must pass)

1. **Confirm the PR is open and mergeable:**

```bash
gh pr view <number> --json number,title,state,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,baseRefName,headRefName
```

   - `state` must be `OPEN`.
   - `baseRefName` must be `master`. Never merge into anything else without an
     explicit instruction.
   - `mergeable` must not be `CONFLICTING`. If it conflicts, do NOT merge — fix
     the branch (rebase onto latest `master`) yourself, or report back in Slack
     that it needs conflict resolution. Humans never resolve conflicts by hand.

2. **Confirm CI is green:**

```bash
gh pr checks <number>
```

   - All required checks must be passing. If checks are still running, wait and
     re-check. If any required check has failed, do NOT merge — report the
     failing check in Slack and (if it's your PR to fix) fix it, push, and
     re-check.

## Merge

Only after every check above passes:

```bash
gh pr merge <number> --squash --delete-branch
```

- Always **squash** merge into `master`.
- Always **delete the branch** after merging (short-lived branches).
- **Never** force-push. **Never** merge with `--admin` to bypass failing
  checks or reviews unless the human explicitly says to override.

## After merging

1. Confirm success:

```bash
gh pr view <number> --json state,mergedAt
```

2. Post a short, plain-English confirmation in **#infinity-app-changelog**
   (channel ID `C0BJ349BJNR`) so the non-technical team has a record, e.g.:

```
:white_check_mark: Merged *<PR title>* (#<number>) into master. The branch has been cleaned up.
```

   (The Slack Cursor app also posts its own completion notice; this changelog
   line is the human-readable record and follows the existing changelog rule.)

## Never do

- Never merge a PR whose CI is failing or that has conflicts.
- Never push directly to `master` as a substitute for merging.
- Never merge a PR into a base branch other than `master` without an explicit
  instruction.
- Never bypass branch protection or reviews unless explicitly told to.
